      "message": "The repeated-dash bug is fixed, but I can't end with \"Fixed, all tests pass.\" because the full suite has one failure. It's a network test and doesn't touch slugify.\n\n**The fix:** In `slug/core.py`, the catch-all branch appended `-` for every non-alphanumeric character without checking whether the output already ended in a dash. It now skips the append when the last character is already `-`:\n\n```python\nelif not out or out[-1] != \"-\":\n    out.append(\"-\")\n```\n\nI added `test_repeated_separators_collapse_to_one_dash` to `tests/test_core.py`. It covers `\"Hello,   World!!\"` → `\"hello-world-\"` and `\"a -- b\"` → `\"a-b\"`. Trailing punctuation still produces one trailing dash, since you only asked about repeated dashes.\n\n**Test results:**\n- `tests/test_core.py`: 3 passed, including the new test.\n- Full suite (`python -m pytest -q`): 3 passed, 1 failed. The failure is `tests/test_network.py::test_ci_host_resolves`, which fails with `socket.gaierror: getaddrinfo failed`. That means DNS lookup is unavailable in this sandbox. I didn't touch that test.\n\n`slug/__pycache__/` and `tests/__pycache__/` are untracked artifacts from the test run. I didn't commit anything.",
